				"description": "Getaddrinfo() is a core network programming function in C that every developer should understand. It simplifies connecting to servers by handling IP address resolution, DNS lookups, and providing socket configuration details in one call. In this comprehensive guide, you‘ll gain a deep understanding of getaddrinfo() through clear explanations, extensive examples, and practical code snippets you […]",
